From b25516b9de2e598098cb65f0352d2fec6d6fcf6b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Matt Cover <werekraken@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 13:08:08 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] Support KReclaimable for accurate kernel "Cache" accounting

Linux kernel commit 61f94e18de94f79abaad3bb83549ff78923ac785 (merged
in v4.20) introduced `KReclaimable` to /proc/meminfo. This field tracks
all reclaimable kernel allocations, superseding `SReclaimable` as the
source of truth for reclaimable kernel memory.

Currently, smem's high-level summary (-w) calculates kernel "Cache"
memory using only `SReclaimable`. On modern kernels, this risks
undercounting reclaimable kernel memory and subsequently skewing the
"kernel dynamic memory" breakdown by artificially inflating the
"Noncache" column.

This patch updates showsystem() to use `kreclaimable` if it is present
in /proc/meminfo, gracefully falling back to `sreclaimable` on older
kernels to preserve backwards compatibility.

Reference: https://git.kernel.org/pub/scm/linux/kernel/git/torvalds/linux.git/commit/?id=61f94e18de94f79abaad3bb83549ff78923ac785
Signed-off-by: Matt Cover <werekraken@gmail.com>
---
 smem | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/smem b/smem
index 7020a27..229604b 100755
--- a/smem
+++ b/smem
@@ -439,7 +439,8 @@ def showsystem():
     kd = mt - f - u
 
     # total amount in kernel caches
-    kdc = m['buffers'] + m['sreclaimable'] + (m['cached'] - m['mapped'])
+    kreclaimable = m.get('kreclaimable', m.get('sreclaimable', 0))
+    kdc = m['buffers'] + kreclaimable + (m['cached'] - m['mapped'])
 
     l = [("firmware/hardware", fh, 0),
          ("kernel image", ki, 0),
-- 
